A||N||2||Diamond Joe Quimby||Engine Stalls||||1||
Z||000000||Diamond Joe Quimby||09-07-2000||04:47 PM||||I have an 84 SE that I am fixing up. When I let it idle for about 15 minutes, it stalls and won't restart for another 10-15 minutes. It is up on jack stands rigth now, so I don't know if the problem exist when driving. I have run the diagnostics, and all I got was code 12 (all is well). I then ran it for 15 or so minutes and it stalled and wouldn't start. I tried to do the diagnostics, and I got nothing at all (the check engine light never even blinked). I also noticed that the check engine light wouldn't come on even if I removed the jumper wire. I continued to try the diagnostic test every 2-3 minutes for about 15 minutes and it never worked. After each attempt, I tried to start the car and it wouldn't start. After about 15 minutes the diagnostic test worked again, but just gave me code 12. When I tried to start the car, it started right up. This has happen several times in a row now<P>Essentially, the car won't start until the diagnostic test works, so I think there is a problem with the ECM heating up or something. Any ideas?<P>Jim S.||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||09-07-2000||07:32 PM||||Ignition controle module and pick up coil in the distributor would most likely be the culprit on a V6...not to sure about a 4 banger though, but its possible.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-08-2000||12:03 AM||||look for battery cable and fuse link problems. (there are some fuse links on the starter in 84. don't forget any.) make sure all the terminals on the starter are tight.<P>then check all the ground ties on the battery, the block, and anyplace else in the engine bay.<P>Yes the ECM could be heating up but check the wiring above first.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-08-2000).]||||reg||1
